  "street_name": "BIGGIN AVENUE",
  "decision_date": "30/09/2025",
  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal by reason of size would fail to provide an acceptable standard of residential accommodation and living space resulting in a cramped and unsatisfactory standard of accommodation to the detriment of the amenities of future occupiers for future occupiers of Flat A and Flat B. The proposal would also fail to provide external amenity space for occupiers of Flat B. The proposal would therefore be contrary to policies London Plan 2021 policy D6, H11.1 and D12.3 of the Merton Local Plan 2024 and the Technical Housing Standards - Nationally Described Space Standard.",
    "Reason : 2 - The development has failed to provide sufficient secure, integrated, convenient and accessible cycle parking facilities, contrary to policy T16.2 of Merton's Local Plan 2024 and T5 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "Reason : 3 - In the absence of adequate refuse and recycling storage facilities for the development, in particular, Flat A, the applicant has not demonstrated that the scheme would safeguard the free flow of traffic in the locality to the detriment of highway and pedestrian safety and safeguard the visual amenity  of the area.  The scheme is contrary to, in particular, Policies D4, SI 7 & SI 8 of the London Plan 2021, Merton Local Plan 2024 policy D12.2, D12.3 and W14.4.",
    "Reason : 4 - The application fails to provide consistent and complete energy and sustainability documentation. While drawings show Air Source Heat Pumps and Solar PV Panels, the Energy Assessment omits PV data and the Energy Statement does not reference them, creating discrepancies. Additionally, the overheating risk assessment lacks clarity and may not meet climate resilience standards. As submitted, the proposal does not demonstrate compliance with Policies CC2.1, CC2.2, CC2.3, CC2.4, and CC2.6 of the Merton Local Plan 2024",
    "Reason : 5 - In the absence of a legal agreement to secure an appropriate contribution towards offsite affordable housing or a satisfactory financial viability assessment to justify the lack of, the scheme fails to address the recognised housing need and will be contrary to, in particular, Policy H11.1 of Merton's Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 6 - In the absence of a noise impact assessment detailing any necessary mitigation measures required with the installation of the Heat Pump, the scheme is considered to harm the residential amenity of nearby occupants contrary to, in particular, Policy P15.10 of Merton Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 7 - In the absence of a Flood Risk Assessment incorporating Sustainable Urban Drainage Design, it has not been demonstrated the scheme would safeguard the risk of flooding in the locality.  The proposal is contrary to, in particular, London Plan 2021 policy SI 13, Merton Local Plan 2024 policies F15.8 and F15.9",
    "Reason : 8 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe application was not considered to comply with the provisions of the Development Plan and NPPF as submitted, and would have required substantial changes such that a new application would be required. \r\n\"\tThe application was considered to be fundamentally contrary to the provisions of the Development Plan and the NPPF, and there were not considered to be any solutions to resolve this conflict. \r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n"
  ],
